  "step_3": "The decision reason evaluates skewness based on the probability of unfavorable outcomes (losses), and specifically prefers the lottery with a greater portion of probability assigned to unfavorable outcomes. In this case, B has 25% chance of loss (vs. A’s 20%), so according to the reason, B should be preferred. However, the individual does not consider the probability of loss at all — they explicitly say that the 20% vs. 25% difference is irrelevant. Instead, they focus solely on the magnitude of the loss: -4000 vs. -3000, and prefer the one with the smaller loss (i.e., B has a smaller loss of -3000). This shows that the individual used a different reasoning — minimizing loss amount — not evaluating skewness or probability distribution of unfavorable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason (based on skewness and probability of unfavorable outcomes) was not used. The individual's justification does not mention probability distribution, skewness, or any comparison based on the proportion of probability on the unfavorable side. The information considered by the individual (loss amount) is different from what is required by the decision reason (probability of unfavorable outcomes). Thus, the reason was not used.",
